{
  "step_1": "The decision reason considers the presence of a sure outcome in each lottery and prefers the lottery with a sure outcome. A 'sure outcome' would be an outcome that occurs with 100% probability. In Lottery A, the outcome '0 Euros' occurs with 99.9% probability, not 100%, so it is not a sure outcome. In Lottery B, '0 Euros' occurs with 99.8% probability, also not 100%. Therefore, neither lottery contains a sure outcome. Since the condition for the decision reason (presence of a sure outcome) is not met in either lottery, the reason cannot be applied to this decision problem. The reason would be indifferent or inapplicable in this case.",
